    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter May 14th with a balanced attack, led by the high-upside pairing of **Kyle Schwarber** (66.38) and **Trea Turner** (65.75). Both benefit significantly from a favorable park factor and a solid matchup against Suarez, who provides a moderate 3.79 xERA. **Yordan Alvarez** (69.34) remains our daily engine, boasting an elite 0.421 xwOBA that helps him transcend the challenge of facing Castillo. While the scarcity of stolen bases remains our primary concern, **Trea Turner**\u2019s dynamic ability against a lefty starter gives him the edge needed to maximize our category footprint today, despite the minor drag of his spot in the lineup.\n\nOur platoon-heavy strategy for this slate highlights **Carson Benge** (62.86), whose favorable pairing against Montero and a +11% boost from SP skill make him a high-efficiency start. Conversely, the benching of **Dillon Dingler** (33.13) was a strictly data-driven outcome. Despite his respectable pedigree, the combination of an elite arm in McLean and a bottom-tier efficiency rating pushed him well below our 40.0 floor, keeping our game caps protected for more favorable windows. We are also monitoring **Casey Schmitt** (44.87) closely; although he occupies a starting spot, his projection relies on an assumed #3 position in the lineup, and any downward shift could force a late-day revaluation. Finally, managers should remain wary of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (41.99), whose aggressive start against Sale is severely hampered by a -15% platoon penalty; he is currently our most volatile asset and sits on the precipice of a benching should the wind or late weather reports shift.",
